1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A boundary changes the movie,
not just dialogue.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
It changes blocking, camera, rhythm,
and cut.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Blocking: change position, distance,
movement, or leave the frame.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Camera: reframe, move away, or stop
recording when the boundary changes.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Rhythm: wait, slow down, or end
the take. Continuity can wait.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Cut: remove an image that no longer
fits the boundary.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
This is a P4 film-craft reading,
not proof of off-camera experience.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
If all four stay fixed,
nothing changes onscreen.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
For the full P4 film essay,
tap the Related video.
